# HAIRPIN on its third course, SUMMIT, at the game's own starting
# settings (HEAVY, 60 pictures a second, CHASE view). Run with --boot off
# --fps 60 --frames 2002.
#
# Home screen: three steps right to the HAIRPIN tile; A (south) at 220
# opens the game. DOWN (250) to COURSE, RIGHT twice (260, 270) from
# RESERVOIR through PINEWOOD to SUMMIT, UP (280) back to PLAY, A (300)
# starts the race.
180 press right
182 release right
186 press right
188 release right
192 press right
194 release right
220 press south
222 release south
250 press down
252 release down
260 press right
262 release right
270 press right
272 release right
280 press up
282 release up
300 press south
302 release south
# From 479 the kart drives itself by these lines: the stick points at
# the middle of the road seen on two rows, A (south) is the throttle and
# is let go, with B (east) as brake, when the road runs far off to one
# side. A closed-loop helper wrote these lines for 30 pictures a second
# by looking at each picture; for 60 each frame number F became 2F - 1
# (the game runs 60 ticks a second at either rate). They are plain
# inputs and replay the same race every time.
# About 1200 to 1520: up to a right hairpin marked with chevrons in the
# snow, braking for it (from 1307), round it and on up through the pines.
479 press south
479 stick left 8000 0
485 stick left 14000 0
485 release south
